From: Reef <reef@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Async player data saving

Inspired by Nitori's / Leaf's "Async playerdata saving".

Player data is still collected on the main thread (it has to be), but
compressing it and writing the .dat file now happen on a single
background thread ("Reef Player Data Saving"). This removes the disk
write from the main thread on autosave and when players quit, which
matters with many players online.

Safety:
- Saves run one at a time, in order, on one thread.
- Writes still go to a temp file that atomically replaces the old one.
- Loading a player's data first waits for any save of that player that
  is still in progress, so a quick quit-and-rejoin never loads old data.
- On shutdown, all pending saves are finished before worlds are saved.
  Saves requested after that run synchronously.

Toggle with optimizations.async-player-data-saving in reef.yml.

